From 8cb1395e27f070094c3a5ced4ac8907e444bd6a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 14:28:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 51/99] HACK: RISC-V: KVM: Expose all counters to VS-mode for
 bootloader compatibility

Some guest bootloaders (e.g. GRUB 2.12, FreeBSD loader) use rdcycle
in grub_efi_get_time_ms() or similar routines. The upstream fix to
use rdtime instead was added in commit c5ae124e11f2 ("kern/riscv/efi/
init: Use time register in grub_efi_get_time_ms()"), but released
versions of these bootloaders do not include this fix.

By default KVM sets hcounteren=0x02, which only allows rdtime to pass
through in VS-mode while rdcycle/rdinstret trap as virtual instructions.
When such bootloaders execute rdcycle, they trap and the guest fails
to boot.

Set hcounteren=0x07 so that VS-mode can access cycle/time/instret
directly without trapping.

Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
---
 arch/riscv/kvm/main.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/kvm/main.c b/arch/riscv/kvm/main.c
index 0f3fe3986fc0..ecc2b8ff700d 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/main.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/main.c
@@ -44,8 +44,16 @@ int kvm_arch_enable_virtualization_cpu(void)
 	csr_write(CSR_HEDELEG, KVM_HEDELEG_DEFAULT);
 	csr_write(CSR_HIDELEG, KVM_HIDELEG_DEFAULT);
 
-	/* VS should access only the time counter directly. Everything else should trap */
-	csr_write(CSR_HCOUNTEREN, 0x02);
+	/*
+	 * HACK: Allow VS-mode to access cycle/time/instret directly.
+	 *
+	 * Some guest bootloaders (e.g. GRUB 2.12, FreeBSD loader) use
+	 * rdcycle for timekeeping and do not include the upstream fix
+	 * (c5ae124e11f2) to use rdtime instead. Expose all counters to
+	 * VS-mode so that guest bootloaders can access cycle/time/instret
+	 * without trapping.
+	 */
+	csr_write(CSR_HCOUNTEREN, 0x07);
 
 	csr_write(CSR_HVIP, 0);
 
